ordinator
>=20
> Hello Yuxia, thanks for your question and interest!
>=20
> When producing, the broker will call the relevant Batch Coordinator wi=
th a
> CommitBatches request.
> The Batch Coordinator will then write the metadata about these batches=
 into
> the __diskless-metadata topic and update its internal state persisted =
on
> SQLite. It will then reply with the assigned offsets.
> Read-only Batch Coordinators will also replicate those metadata into t=
heir
> own internal state.
>=20
> When consuming, the broker will call the relevant Batch Coordinator wi=
th a
> FindBatches request.
> The Batch Coordinator will search the requested offsets within its int=
ernal
> state and reply with the batch coordinates (object key, offset within =
the
> object).
>=20
> In your example, I suppose that A, B and C are all messages written to=
 the
> same topic-partition.
