Hello Sanghyeok An,

Thanks for the feedback,

The consumer already has corresponding close semantics that =
differentiate behavior=20
based on membership, and in that context I agree that having static =
members remain in the group=20
by default is reasonable and consistent with the goal of static =
membership.=20

Based on this, I plan to make the behavior explicit in the KIP: under =
the Streams Protocol,=20
CloseOptions.DEFAULT will resolve to remain in group for static members, =
while keeping=20
the existing behavior for dynamic members.

Best Regards,
Jiunn-Yang

> Sanghyeok An <ojt90902@naver.com> =E6=96=BC 2026=E5=B9=B42=E6=9C=8827=E6=
=97=A5 =E6=99=9A=E4=B8=8A10:57 =E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
>=20
> Hi Jiunn-Yang,
> Thanks for the this KIP.=20
>=20
> I have a small question.
>=20
> ash01 :=20
> Would it be worth considering mapping CloseOptions.DEFAULT differently =
not only based on the protocol, but also on whether the member is =
static?
>=20
> I recently worked on a server-side implementation of static membership =
for KIP-1071.=20
> Once static members are supported under the Streams Protocol, DEFAULT =
close semantics may reasonably differ between dynamic and static =
members.
>=20
> For dynamic members, I agree with the KIP rationale that remaining in =
the group provides no real benefit, so having DEFAULT map to a leave =
behavior under the Streams Protocol makes sense.=20
> However, for static members, making leave the default would weaken the =
primary benefit of static membership, minimizing rebalances on restart.
>=20
> Would it make sense to resolve DEFAULT under the Streams Protocol as =
follows?
> - dynamic member: DEFAULT maps to consumer CloseOptions.DEFAULT =
(leave)
> - static member: DEFAULT maps to consumer CloseOptions.REMAIN_IN_GROUP =
(remain)
>=20
> This would keep the no-arg KafkaStreams.close() as a safer default in =
both cases, while still reserving REMAIN_IN_GROUP as an explicit user =
intent.
> Curious what you think, and whether this should be in scope for this =
KIP or tracked as a follow-up.
>=20
> Thanks for reading this!=20
>=20
> Best Regards
> Sanghyeok An
>=20
