Hi everyone,
I would like to start the discussion on a proposed KIP related to KAFKA-136=
78.
This idea follows the suggestion in the JIRA discussion to extend the exist=
ing scheduling mechanism with a time-shift parameter rather than introducin=
g a new abstraction. The goal is to allow globally aligned scheduling while=
 keeping the API simple and consistent with current semantics.
The draft KIP is available here:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1293%3A+Add+Time-Shif=
t+Parameter+to+Kafka+Streams+Punctuation+Scheduling
The JIRA is here:
https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-13678
Looking forward to your thoughts and suggestions.
Thanks,
Ankur


