> Thanks for the feedback,
> 
> The consumer already has corresponding close semantics that differentiate behavior
> based on membership, and in that context I agree that having static members remain in the group
> by default is reasonable and consistent with the goal of static membership.
> 
> Based on this, I plan to make the behavior explicit in the KIP: under the Streams Protocol,
> CloseOptions.DEFAULT will resolve to remain in group for static members, while keeping
> the existing behavior for dynamic members.
> 
