> Hey folks,
>
> We here at LinkedIn are on our journey to move to Northguard and as such =
our participation with Apache Kafka has lessened over the years. Despite no=
t actively contributing to Kafka anymore, we have developed and maintained =
Kafka Cruise Control and made it available to the community which has gaine=
d wide adoption across the users of Kafka.
>
> As we move further towards full Northguard adoption and our Kafka footpri=
nt shrinks, we also have made less investment in the Cruise Control project=
 as well. However, we don't want to let the project die within LinkedIn and=
 force a community fork. As such, we want to investigate relieving ourselve=
s of ownership and donating Cruise Control. We believe Apache Kafka is like=
ly the right spot for this overall to maintain close continuity with the co=
re Kafka project.
>
> We'd like to begin a conversation on this and discuss what the process wo=
uld look like compared to other open source options. We have had discussion=
s in the past with Linux Foundation as well. If you could help identify who=
'd be the right contact to start discussions with, I'd appreciate it!
>
> Thanks,
>
> Krit Petty,
> Sr. Manager, Kafka, LinkedIn
