	charset=utf-8

Thanks for the KIP.=20

I do acknowledge that there could be gap with the =E2=80=9Clatest=E2=80=9D=
 setting and it could be addressed differently rather than having =
=E2=80=9Cearliest" offset settings.=20
I was going through the KIP and had few comments or was not fully clear =
on the proposed solution=20
If consumer restarts (app crash, bounce etc.) after dynamically adding =
partitions it would consume unread messages from last committed offset =
for existing partitions but would still miss the messages from new =
partition. =20
If the offset are deleted mention in mentioned in Scenario 2 (Log =
truncation) how this solution would address that scenario ?
Do we need to care about Clock Skew or SystemTime Issues on consumer =
client side. Should we use timestamp on the server/broker side ?
Do you plan to have any metrics or observability when consumer resets =
offset by_start_time =20


> On Mar 5, 2026, at 06:14, =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD =
<s7133700@gmail.com> wrote:
>=20
> Hello everyone,=20
>=20
> I would like to start a discussion on KIP-1282: Prevent data loss =
during partition expansion for dynamically added partitions
> <https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/mIY8G>
>=20
> This proposal aims to introduce a new auto.offset.reset policy =
by_start_time, anchoring the=20
> offset reset to the consumer's startup timestamp rather than partition =
discovery time, to prevent=20
> silent data loss during partition expansion.
>=20
> Best regards,
> Jiunn-Yang


