Subject: [VOTE]KIP-1266: Bounding The Number Of RemoteLogMetadata Messages via
 Compacted Topic
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="000000000000fdf8b1064c518936"
From: Lijun Tong <shelijun.tong@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

--000000000000fdf8b1064c518936
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi,

I'd like to start a vote on KIP-1266 which proposes to turn the current
remote log metadata topic for the tiered storage to compacted topic, to
limit the number of messages that need to be iterated to build the remote
metadata state and remove the burden to tune the retention time for this
topic when operating the tiered storage.

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1266%3A+Bounding+The+Number+Of+RemoteLogMetadata+Messages+via+Compacted+Topic


Let me know if you have any feedback.

Thanks,
Lijun Tong

--000000000000fdf8b1064c518936--

