> epoch N, then the 2 clusters can sync up successfully.
> And that's why I proposed to the "last mirrored leader epoch" semantic in
> the sub-proposal
> <
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/Unclean+Leader+Election=
+in+Cluster+Mirroring
> >,
> which is a solution to draw a line between these 2 clusters to declare
> records beyond the "last mirrored leader epoch" N, it belongs to who. I
> think this should work well, as long as all replicas in the cluster can
> truncate the log correctly.
>
> What do you think?
>
> Any feedback is appreciated.
>
> Thank you,
> Luke
