Hi Dongjin and Kafka devs,

I would like to revive this thread since it seems to have gone stale. There
appears to be growing demand for exposing such options (e.g., the recently
added ZSTD options: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/21568).

I still believe making these options available would be beneficial for the
community.

To answer your question Dongjin:

DL1: yes, we can easily update it not sure what you mean by options (as
those are already updates) but I assume you meant primary add co-proposer.
Yeah I am fine with that.

DL2: sure, if you have spare time go ahead. If you are currently busy I can
do it so ... (but anyway we should first see from PMCs if this is something
they would like to have).

DL3: cool, adding more dataset would be really good to see how those
options can change those metrics (e.g., throughput or compression ratio).

Cheers,

Maros

