Hi Ryan,

That is a fantastic point. A static member restarting and capturing a newer l=
ocal timestamp is definitely a critical edge case.

Since users already need to inject a unique group.instance.id into the config=
uration for static members, my idea is to allow the auto.offset.reset policy =
to carry a dedicated timestamp to explicitly "lock" the startup time (for exa=
mple, using a format like auto.offset.reset=3Dstartup:<timestamp>).

This means that if users want to leverage this new policy with static members=
hip, their deployment configuration would simply include these two specific i=
njected values (the static ID and the locked timestamp).

This approach elegantly maintains the configuration semantics at the member-l=
evel, and most importantly, it avoids any need to update the RPC protocol.

What do you think of this approach for the static membership scenario?

On 2026/03/05 19:45:13 "Ryan Leslie (BLOOMBERG/ NEW YORK)" wrote:
