newer local timestamp is definitely a critical edge case.
>=20
> Since users already need to inject a unique group.instance.id into the =
configuration for static members, my idea is to allow the =
auto.offset.reset policy to carry a dedicated timestamp to explicitly =
"lock" the startup time (for example, using a format like =
auto.offset.reset=3Dstartup:<timestamp>).
>=20
> This means that if users want to leverage this new policy with static =
membership, their deployment configuration would simply include these =
two specific injected values (the static ID and the locked timestamp).
>=20
