>>> I just wanted to make sure I=E2=80=99m on the right track, so I=E2=80=99=
m sharing my
>>> understanding of
>>> the current process for adding a controller to the voter set.
>>>=20
>>> Here's what I think it looks like:
>>> Step 1: Use kafka-storage.sh format to format the controller.
>>> Step 2: Start up the controller and ensure it starts up =
successfully.
>>> Step 3: Provide the controller config and use the =
kafka-metadata-quorum.sh
>>> add-controller command to add the controller to the voter set.
>>>=20
>>> The KIP aims to simplify "Step 3". It removes the need to provide =
the
>>> controller config,
>>> as all the information that add-controller requires=E2=80=94like the =
directory UUID
>>> and controller endpoint=E2=80=94
>>> can be gathered through Admin#describeMetadataQuorum and
>>> Admin#describeConfigs.
>>> Since the controller is already in the cluster by Step 2, this =
information
>>> should be available.
>>>=20
>>> So, users would still need to complete "Step 1" and "Step 2".
>>> Otherwise, as you mentioned, we won=E2=80=99t be able to retrieve =
the controller
>>> UUID and its corresponding endpoints for Step 3.
>>>=20
>>> I=E2=80=99m not sure if I=E2=80=99ve misunderstood anything, so =
please let me know if
>>> there=E2=80=99s anything I=E2=80=99ve missed.
>>>=20
>>> Thanks so much for reviewing my KIP!
>>>=20
>>> Best regards,
>>> Kuan-Po Tseng
>>>=20
