>>>> - The most obvious way to do that is to format the new controller =
node
>>>> first, and then grab that ID. This is what the current system does, =
by
>>>> reading that local file.
>>>>=20
>>>> - Another way to do it would be to generate the UUID somewhere =
else, and
>>>> then format using --initial-controllers. This currently requires =
spelling
>>>> out the full set of controllers and matching directory ids in the
>>> cluster.
>>>> One thing that is a bit subtle is that the tool will actually look =
at
>>> what
>>>> directory ID you gave, and use that directory ID when formatting =
your
>>>> directory. This should be documented a bit more prominently if we =
want
>>>> people to use this mechanism.
>>>>=20
>>>> best,
>>>> Colin
