Hi kafka-connect folks,

READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS is currently hardcoded as 30 second in kafka-co=
nnect's=C2=A0KafkaConfigBackingStore.java (https://github.com/a0x8o/kafka/b=
lob/master/connect/runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/connect/storage/K=
afkaConfigBackingStore.java#L244). =C2=A0This parameter is used to control =
the upper bound time we allowed to write configuration changes to the kafka=
-connect's config.storage topic (and this topic is usually configured as on=
e-partition topic)

We have topics with more than 500 partitions and the connector tasks of mor=
e than 500 (one task for each kafka partition). =C2=A0When the consumer reb=
alance happens, kafka-connect code needs to finish the writing of all task =
configs into the config.storage topic within=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_=
MS and sometimes it is not enough time.

Can we increase=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS to a larger value e.g. 300=
 seconds? =C2=A0Or better to make it a configurable parameter?

