Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20307) Add Interactive Queries (IQv1)
 support for headers-aware stores
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Alieh Saeedi (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Alieh Saeedi created KAFKA-20307:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Add Interactive Queries (IQv1) support for headers-aw=
are stores
                 Key: KAFKA-20307
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20307
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Alieh Saeedi


=C2=A0Problem

The new headers-aware state stores (TimestampedKeyValueStoreWithHeaders and=
 TimestampedWindowStoreWithHeaders) cannot be queried using the existing In=
teractive Queries v1 (IQv1) API. Users attempting to query these stores via=
 QueryableStoreTypes.keyValueStore() or QueryableStoreTypes.timestampedKeyV=
alueStore() will fail because QueryableStoreTypes doesn't recognize headers=
-aware stores as valid store types
=C2=A0 2. State restoration doesn't know which format to use for headers-aw=
are stores

=C2=A0 Proposed Solution

=C2=A0 Enable backward compatibility by:

=C2=A0 1. Store Type Recognition - Update QueryableStoreTypes to accept hea=
ders-aware stores
=C2=A0 2. Automatic Facade Wrapping - Modify GlobalStateStoreProvider and S=
treamThreadStateStoreProvider to wrap headers-aware stores with facades tha=
t strip headers/timestamps as needed
=C2=A0 3. Restoration Support - Add StateManagerUtil.converterForStore() to=
 determine correct restoration format for any store type
=C2=A0 4. Read-Only Decorator - Add decorator for headers-aware stores to p=
revent writes during queries

=C2=A0 Expected Behavior

=C2=A0 Users can query headers-aware stores using existing IQv1 code withou=
t modifications:
=C2=A0 - keyValueStore() =E2=86=92 returns plain values (headers and timest=
amps stripped)
=C2=A0 - timestampedKeyValueStore() =E2=86=92 returns ValueAndTimestamp<V> =
(headers stripped)
=C2=A0 - windowStore() =E2=86=92 returns plain values (headers and timestam=
ps stripped)
=C2=A0 - timestampedWindowStore() =E2=86=92 returns ValueAndTimestamp<V> (h=
eaders stripped)

=C2=A0

=C2=A0



