Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi Kafka Dev Team,

My name is Yeojun Kim, and I am a software engineer interested in
contributing to Apache Kafka. I have been following the project for some
time and would love to start helping out.

As I am new to the codebase, I am looking for a *"Good First Issue"* to get
familiar with the contribution workflow. I am particularly interested in *small
bug fixes, documentation improvements, or minor refactorings.*

I have experience in *Java and distributed systems,* and I am currently in
the final stages of a contribution to the *Armeria project* (my PR is
nearing merge after a successful review process). This experience has made
me well-versed in the open-source workflow, from issue analysis to
addressing code review feedback.

If there are any pending tasks suitable for a first-time contributor, could
you please point me in the right direction?

Thanks in advance for your guidance!

Best regards, Yeojun Kim

*P.S.* For your reference, here is a link to my recent PR in the Armeria
project, which is currently undergoing the final stages of the review
process: Armeria PR Link <https://github.com/line/armeria/pull/6603>

