Hi Mickael,

About KIP-1274, it was mainly about alignment on a path forward. The only
change shipping in 4.3 is a new log line really. We wanted to wait for some
related fixes to go in the release before adding it though (in-flight PRs
in review, expected to meet code-freeze), all linked in the KIP jira for
4.3 https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20282

Given this slightly different case only adding a log line, I expect it
should be ok to just add the change before the code freeze deadline, and
still consider the KIP part of the release. Makes sense?

Thanks!
Lianet

