Hi all,

Thanks for the discussions and votes. Since there are already two +1s, I
wanted to make all aware that I made some updates to the design as a result
of the discussion here:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/otqp124y3h6h9fl2zg9fklg036r50mvs
The main change is that I believe it is fine to relax the formatting
requirements further to no longer include "bootstrap" controllers. This
means this feature supports skipping formatting on all nodes. A consequence
of this is the initial active controller might not have cluster.id in its
meta.properties, and therefore needs to generate one as part of the
bootstrap metadata write.

Please take a look at the changes:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1262%3A+Enable+auto-f=
ormatting+directories
and let me know if you have any questions.

Best,
Kevin Wu

