Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-20367:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Support Share Groups (Queue Semantics) in Kafka Conne=
ct Sink Connectors
                 Key: KAFKA-20367
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20367
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
          Components: connect, consumer, group-coordinator, kip
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak
            Assignee: Shekhar Prasad Rajak


Introduce Share Group support in Kafka Connect sink tasks via a new WorkerS=
hareSinkTask, enabling queue semantics (record-level distribution, no rebal=
ances) with config-only opt=E2=80=91in.=20

At=E2=80=91least=E2=80=91once is default;=20
exactly=E2=80=91once is supported only for same=E2=80=91cluster Kafka=E2=80=
=91to=E2=80=91Kafka when KIP=E2=80=911289 transactional share acknowledgmen=
ts are available.=20

Error handling uses RELEASE for retriable failures and REJECT for fatal fai=
lures; when KIP=E2=80=911191 is enabled, broker=E2=80=91side DLQ is the sol=
e DLQ source (Connect does not emit its own DLQ records in Share Group mode=
).




