Hi Ashwin,
Yes, we should have a note that=C2=A0 share groups are only suitable for co=
nnectors with=C2=A0idempotent, order-independent=C2=A0processing.
About switching to share group protocol:=C2=A0Share groups use a different =
state topic (__share_group_state), but looks like=C2=A0__consumer_offsets=
=C2=A0will be used for memebership, so if we do not delete the group before=
 switching it can cause problem.
Thanks, let me update.=C2=A0
Best,Shekhar

=20

    On Tuesday 31 March 2026 at 02:33:02 pm GMT+5:30, Ashwin via dev <dev@k=
afka.apache.org> wrote: =20
=20
 Hi Shekhar,

Thanks for the KIP.

I was wondering if you could also add a section on how message ordering can
no longer be guaranteed at partition level ? Some connectors (eg: JDBC
sink) rely on ordering of messages in a topic partition to set the values
correctly in the sink system. How do we protect users from turning this
feature on for a connector which requires ordering ?

 If we want to support changing the consumer group type for a running
connector, we may have to change the default group name as it may clash
with the previous group.

Thanks,
Ashwin

